     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear all,<br><br>Firstly thank you to the developers of both the unmarked and AICcmodavg packages and to the group. The posts have been really useful in developing my script. <br>I have a problem which may not be directly relevant to the group as it may be to do with AICcmodavg rather than unmarked, so please remove if inappropriate. <br><br>I have been running N-mixture models using pcount in unmarked on a stacked/pooled two year data set of snake counts from 23 sites with up to 8 replicates. In order to assess the most appropriate mixture I ran each (P,NB,ZIP) for the top selected and null models and then selected that with the lowest AICc (shown in bold) as calculated using Nmix.gof.test (AICcmodavg package) with 1000 simulations. As I am interested in the abundance rather than detection in this instance n set to the number of sites (23) was preferential, and so have been using the Negative Binomial mixture. As you can see from the table below despite other statistics indicating best fit, we got a c-hat of 0 indicating massive underdispersion (actual value = 6.22E-13). <br><br>\r\n\r\n<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;border:none\" width=\"548\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\">\r\n <tbody><tr style=\"height:1.0cm\">\r\n  <td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"width:70.85pt;border-top:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-left:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:none;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;height:1.0cm\" width=\"94\">\r\n  <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0cm;line-height:normal\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\">Models</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"width:61.25pt;border-top:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-left:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;border-right:none;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;height:1.0cm\" width=\"82\">\r\n  <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;text-align:center;text-indent:.05pt;line-height:norma