   "subject": "Re: Underdispersion of negative binomial model (0) with Nmix.gof.test (AICcmodavg)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi John and Marc,<br><br>Thanks for your replies and comments. Just to clarify the n=162 is sites (23) x replicates (8) with missing surveys removed (i.e. some sites were padded with NAs where less replicates occurred). As I&#39;m using AICc rather than AIC to assess goodness of fit due to small sample size I tested the models with n set to both just to see if there was much difference in the model selection.<br><br>I has previously read the references you suggest, and I thank you for drawing me back to them as they do make some very interesting points which I had not considered when addressing the underdispersion issue. Based on this and your comments I will move forward with the Poisson mixture and see if that gives me ecologically sensible estimates. <br><br>I greatly appreciate your time and will also pass your comments on to my friendly neighbourhood statistical ecologist who was interested in the outcome of this.<br><br>Many thanks,<br><br>Rob<br><br><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
